course: dictionary
lesson: 8641
title: Seafaring
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Seafaring is a describing word (an adjective), and it can also be a naming word (a noun). Break it into two parts: sea and faring. Faring is an old word for travelling, so seafaring is about travelling or working on the sea.
explain: Look at the clues in the sentence: «I'm a seafaring rat, I am, and the port I originally hail from is Constantinople.» A port is a place where ships arrive, so this rat has travelled by sea. Try a test: swap in a word you know, like "sailing rat". It still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: As a noun, seafaring means the life or work of sailors, or travel by sea. You do not add an s to it, because it is an uncountable noun. A seafarer is a person who makes their living at sea.
fact: Seafaring means working or travelling on the sea.
fact: As a noun, seafaring means the life or work of sailors.
fact: A seafarer is a sailor.
fact: The Vikings and Polynesians were great seafaring peoples, so they were skilled at sailing long distances.
fact: In «The Wind in the Willows», the Sea Rat is a seafaring rat who tells the Water Rat tales of faraway ports.
exercise: «The Vikings were a seafaring people.» What does seafaring mean? | Living high in the mountains | Hiding from the rain | *Working or travelling on the sea | Growing crops on a farm
exercise: The Sea Rat says the port he hails from is Constantinople. What does hail from mean? | Shout to | Be afraid of | *Come from | Sail away from
exercise: A seafarer is a person who is a | baker | *sailor | teacher | gardener
test: In the sentence «Seafaring has shaped his whole life», what does seafaring mean? | A kind of song | A long walk on land | A type of boat | *The life and work of sailors
test: Which word is closest in meaning to seafaring as an adjective? | *Maritime | Mountain | Landlocked | Desert
exam: Based on «a seafaring rat» and the port of Constantinople, what kind of life has the Sea Rat lived? | A life underground | A life in a city far from any water | A quiet life on a farm | *A life of sailing and travel by sea
